# XSH setkey()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Obsolescent. The algorithm is implementation-defined; only the ignored bits and errno are checked.

assertion  XSH.setkey.001
anchor     functions/setkey.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI+CRYPT
says       In each group of 8 elements of the key the low-order bit is ignored:
           inverting that element in every group leaves the encoding of a block
           unchanged.
note       The page does not say whether the low-order element is the first or
           the last of a group; either is accepted (the encoding is unchanged for
           one of the two choices). ENOSYS gives NOTINUSE.
test       t/001-parity.c

assertion  XSH.setkey.002
anchor     functions/setkey.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI+CRYPT
says       setkey() does not change errno when it succeeds.
note       ENOSYS gives NOTINUSE.
test       t/002-errno.c
